---
title: "Cheat sheet"
description: "Every construct on one page: front matter, cells, divs, references and shortcodes, with a link to the chapter that explains each."
---

*Reference: Cheat sheet · [CLI](cli.tmd) · [Configuration](frontmatter.tmd) · [Cell options](cell-options.tmd) · [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.tmd) · [Accessibility](accessibility.tmd) · [Licensing](licensing.tmd)*

Every construct taliesin supports fits in the seven tables below. Anything you can
write that is not named on this page is either plain CommonMark, which just works,
or not something taliesin implements.

## Front matter

| Key | What it does | Chapter |
|---|---|---|
| `title:` | The document title: drives `<title>`, the title block, and social meta | [Configuration reference](frontmatter.tmd#document-front-matter) |
| `subtitle:` | A secondary line under the title | [Configuration reference](frontmatter.tmd#document-front-matter) |
| `author:` | A name, a list of names, or a structured list with affiliations | [Configuration reference](frontmatter.tmd#sec-authors) |
| `date:` | Publication date; sorts a `listing:` | [Configuration reference](frontmatter.tmd#document-front-matter) |
| `description:` | Summary for the meta description and the social-share unfurl | [Configuration reference](frontmatter.tmd#document-front-matter) |
| `categories:` | Tags for the page; each becomes a `<category>` in the Atom feed | [Configuration reference](frontmatter.tmd#document-front-matter) |
| `page-layout:` | `full` widens the content column (for a listing index); the default is the reading-width column | [Configuration reference](frontmatter.tmd#document-front-matter) |
| `image:` | The picture on a `listing:` card and the `og:image` a shared link unfurls with | [Configuration reference](frontmatter.tmd#document-front-matter) |
| `image-alt:` | The `alt` text for that picture; required whenever `image:` is set | [Configuration reference](frontmatter.tmd#document-front-matter) |
| `draft:` | Holds a page out of the build; the preview still shows it, badged | [Configuration reference](frontmatter.tmd#document-front-matter) |
| `title-block-style:` | `none` hides the visible `<h1>` title block (the title still drives `<title>`, OpenGraph, nav) | [Configuration reference](frontmatter.tmd#document-front-matter) |
| `toc:` | Forces the table of contents on or off (automatic by default) | [Configuration reference](frontmatter.tmd#document-front-matter) |
| `bibliography:` | A `.bib` file, enabling `[@key]` citations | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#citations-and-cross-references) |
| `execute:` | Document-wide cell defaults (`cache:`) | [Configuration reference](frontmatter.tmd#execute-document-wide-cell-defaults) |
| `listing:` | Turns the page into an index: a card per document | [Configuration reference](frontmatter.tmd#listing-an-index-page) |
| `hero:` | A landing-page banner with a headline and call-to-action buttons | [Configuration reference](frontmatter.tmd#hero-a-landing-banner) |

That is every top-level front-matter key taliesin recognizes except `csl`, which is
left off on purpose: it is recognized but not honoured (the build warns and does
nothing), so there is no behavior to document. See [Configuration
reference](frontmatter.tmd#document-front-matter).

## Cells

| Syntax | What it does | Chapter |
|---|---|---|
| `{python}` | Executes against a warm Jupyter kernel | [Executable content](../using/code.tmd#code-cells) |
| `{js}` | Runs in the browser, wired into the reactive graph | [Interactive documents](../using/interactive.tmd#reactive-js-cells) |
| `{mermaid}` | Renders a diagram client-side | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#diagrams) |
| `{=html}` | Raw HTML, emitted verbatim | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#raw-html-passthrough) |
| `{bash}` `{sql}` `{julia}` `{rust}` | Highlighted, never executed. Unlike a plain ` ```bash ` fence these take `#\|` options, so a `label:` plus `lst-cap:` turns one into a numbered listing | [Executable content](../using/code.tmd#code-cells) |
| `#\|` | Leading cell-option prefix (most languages) | [Cell-options reference](cell-options.tmd#how-options-are-written) |
| `//\|` | Leading cell-option prefix (`{js}`) | [Cell-options reference](cell-options.tmd#how-options-are-written) |
| `%%\|` | Leading cell-option prefix (`{mermaid}`) | [Cell-options reference](cell-options.tmd#how-options-are-written) |

## Cell options

| Option | What it does | Chapter |
|---|---|---|
| `#\| echo:` | `false` hides the source listing; the cell still runs | [Cell-options reference](cell-options.tmd#every-option) |
| `#\| include:` | `false` hides both source and output | [Cell-options reference](cell-options.tmd#every-option) |
| `#\| cache:` | `false` opts the cell out of the `_freeze/` cache | [Cell-options reference](cell-options.tmd#every-option) |
| `#\| label:` | A `fig-`/`lst-`/`tbl-` name makes the output numbered and cross-referenceable | [Cell-options reference](cell-options.tmd#every-option) |
| `#\| fig-cap:` | A caption that makes the output a numbered figure | [Cell-options reference](cell-options.tmd#every-option) |
| `#\| lst-cap:` | A caption that makes the source a numbered listing | [Cell-options reference](cell-options.tmd#every-option) |
| `#\| tbl-cap:` | A caption that makes the output a numbered table | [Cell-options reference](cell-options.tmd#every-option) |
| `#\| code-fold:` | Collapses the listing into a closed (or, with `show`, open) `<details>` | [Cell-options reference](cell-options.tmd#every-option) |
| `#\| code-summary:` | The label on a folded listing | [Cell-options reference](cell-options.tmd#every-option) |
| `//\| name:` | Publishes a `{js}` cell's return value under this name | [Cell-options reference](cell-options.tmd#js-reactive-options) |
| `//\| viewof:` | The cell returns a DOM input registered under this name | [Cell-options reference](cell-options.tmd#js-reactive-options) |
| `//\| input:` | Comma-separated names this cell re-runs on | [Cell-options reference](cell-options.tmd#js-reactive-options) |

## Divs

| Syntax | What it does | Chapter |
|---|---|---|
| `::: {.callout-note}` | An informational aside | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#callouts) |
| `::: {.callout-tip}` | A tip or a recommendation | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#callouts) |
| `::: {.callout-warning}` | A caution the reader should not skip | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#callouts) |
| `::: {.column-margin}` | Floats into the right margin on a wide screen, folds into the flow on a narrow one | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#footnotes-and-sidenotes) |
| `::: {.column-page}` | Widens a block up to the page width | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#footnotes-and-sidenotes) |

**Three attributes go inside the braces.** `title="…"` sets a callout's heading (else a
leading heading, else the kind) and `collapse="true"` folds it into a native `<details>`
(`"false"` starts it open); both are callout-only. `layout-ncol=3` lays a **plain** div's
blocks out as an N-column grid. Any class this table does not name is passed straight
through to the `<div>` for your own CSS, and is not diagnosed.

## Math

| Syntax | What it does | Chapter |
|---|---|---|
| `$…$` | Inline math, in running text | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#math) |
| `$$…$$` | Display math, standing on its own | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#math) |
| `$$…$$ {#eq-x}` | A **numbered** display equation, cross-referenceable as `@eq-x` | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#math) |

All three render server-side with KaTeX at build time, fonts inlined, so a built page
needs no network. The last row is the one worth seeing: @eq-cheat below is written that
way, and this sentence references it.

$$
e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0
$$ {#eq-cheat}

## References

| Syntax | What it does | Chapter |
|---|---|---|
| `[@key]` | A citation, resolved against `bibliography:` | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#citations-and-cross-references) |
| `@fig-name` | Cross-reference to a numbered figure | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#citations-and-cross-references) |
| `@sec-name` | Cross-reference to a heading carrying `{#sec-name}` | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#citations-and-cross-references) |
| `@tbl-name` | Cross-reference to a numbered table | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#citations-and-cross-references) |
| `@eq-name` | Cross-reference to a numbered equation | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#citations-and-cross-references) |
| `@lst-name` | Cross-reference to a numbered listing | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#citations-and-cross-references) |
| `[^label]` | A footnote, rendered as a margin sidenote next to the line that cites it | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#footnotes-and-sidenotes) |
| `{#anchor}` | An explicit id on a heading, figure, or equation, for an `@`-reference to target | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#citations-and-cross-references) |

## Shortcodes

| Syntax | What it does | Chapter |
|---|---|---|
| `{{< include path/to/partial.tmd >}}` | Splices another file's contents in before parsing | [Rich writing](../using/writing.tmd#reusing-a-partial) |
| `{{< input name="k" type="slider" >}}` | A labelled, keyboard-accessible control (`slider`, `number`, `checkbox`, `text`, or `select`) wired into the reactive graph | [Interactive documents](../using/interactive.tmd#inputs-without-boilerplate-input) |
